  "extraction_notes": "[text-pass] The article focuses on Ba2.75Pb1.1Sb4.1Se10-\u03b4Te\u03b4. The parent compound (\u03b4=0) and \u03b4=1 were too resistive for high-temperature TE measurements. Data for \u03b4=2, 3, and 4 were extracted from the text. ZT for \u03b4=2 is stated as 'almost zero' at 773 K. [figure-pass p1-5] The provided document discusses a new quaternary selenide material, Ba2.75Pb1.1Sb4.1Se10, and its Te-doped derivatives. It does not contain any data or plots for AgSbTe2-family compounds. [figure-pass p6-10] The paper discusses Ba2.75Pb1.1Sb4.1Se10-deltaTed compounds. While AgSbTe2 is mentioned as a reference material for low thermal conductivity, the primary materials studied are the Ba-Pb-Sb-Se-Te system. No thermoelectric data for AgSbTe2 itself was extracted as it was only cited as a comparison. [figure-pass p11-13] The provided pages discuss a Ba-Pb-Sb-Se-Te system (Ba2.75Pb1.1Sb4.1Se10-deltaTe_delta). This is not an AgSbTe2-family compound. Therefore, no relevant data for the requested family was extracted. ",
